    "q-100794": {
      "dom_id": "step-q100794",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What is the product of solutions of the equation $3{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x}=11x\\cdot {5}^{x}+4\\cdot {5}^{x}?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor the equation:\n\n  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x} & =11x\\cdot {5}^{x}+4\\cdot {5}^{x} \\\\ 3{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x}-11x\\cdot {5}^{x}-4\\cdot {5}^{x} & =0 \\\\ (3{x}^{2}-11x-4)\\cdot {5}^{x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}-11x-4=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{5}^{x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $3{x}^{2}-11x-4=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(3x+1)(x-4)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-\\frac{1}{3},4.$\n\n- The equation ${5}^{x}=0$ has no solutions because ${5}^{x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-\\frac{1}{3},4,$ and their product is $(-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 4=-\\frac{4}{3}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
