    "q-100799": {
      "dom_id": "step-q100799",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "What is the product of solutions of the equation $9{x}^{2}{e}^{x}=36{e}^{x}?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}{e}^{x} & =36{e}^{x} \\\\ 9{x}^{2}{e}^{x}-36{e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ (9{x}^{2}-36){e}^{x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}-36=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{e}^{x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $9{x}^{2}-36=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(3x+6)(3x-6)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-2,2.$\n\n- The equation ${e}^{x}=0$ has no solutions because ${e}^{x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-2,2,$ and their product is $(-2)\\cdot 2=-4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
